# BEGIN app-configs syncthing obsidian ignore

# Syncthing ignore rules for Obsidian metadata in any synced folder.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# Obsidian writes per-device UI/runtime state into `.obsidian/` and rewrites it
# constantly and independently on every machine. Syncing those files makes
# Syncthing race against itself and spew conflict files forever. Ignoring every
# `.obsidian/` folder keeps notes syncing while making Obsidian settings local.
#
# HOW SYNCTHING USES THIS FILE
# Syncthing reads `.stignore` from each synced folder root. With the leading
# `(?d)` flag, ignored files are ALSO deletable so a leftover conflict file on
# one device does not get re-propagated. Install this managed block on every
# configured Syncthing folder (see ops/syncthing-obsidian-stignore.sh).
#
# Patterns are relative to the folder root. `**` matches across directories.

# --- Never sync Obsidian metadata folders anywhere in a Syncthing folder ----
(?d).obsidian
(?d).obsidian/**
(?d)**/.obsidian
(?d)**/.obsidian/**

# --- Always drop any conflict files Syncthing already produced -------------
(?d)**.sync-conflict-*
(?d)**sync-conflict-*
(?d)**data-sync-conflict.*

# --- Common cross-tool noise ------------------------------------------------
(?d)**/.DS_Store
(?d)**/Thumbs.db

# END app-configs syncthing obsidian ignore
